/**
\page page_stfpdcollection StFpdCollection — FPD Legacy Raw-Data Collection

\section fpd_overview Overview

\ref StFpdCollection is the legacy raw-data container for the
<b>Forward Pion Detector (FPD)</b>, the predecessor to the FMS.  The FPD consisted
of four lead-glass calorimeter modules (North, South, Top, Bottom), shower-maximum
detectors (SMD x and y strip arrays), pre-shower scintillator layers, and a set of
PMTs shared with the EEMC.

Unlike the more recent collection classes, \ref StFpdCollection stores raw hardware-
level quantities — ADC counts, TDC values, pedestals, scalers, and an event token —
rather than reconstructed physics objects.  All arrays are fixed-size members; there
is no dynamic allocation.

\section fpd_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StFpdCollection contains no heap-allocated objects.  All data arrays are plain
C arrays embedded in the object.  The collection is owned by \ref StEvent, managed
by the \c St_DataSet/StXRefMain framework.

\section fpd_arraycaps Array Capacities

| Constant | Value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mMaxAdc | 256 | Total ADC channels (all sub-detectors multiplexed). |
| \c mMaxTdc | 8 | TDC channels. |
| \c mMaxRegisters | 3 | Hardware register values. |
| \c mMaxPedestal | 256 | Pedestal values. |
| \c mMaxPMTpEEMC | 12 | PMTs shared with EEMC (North, PreShower1/2). |
| \c mMaxPMTPbg | 16 | Lead-glass PMTs (South, Top, Bottom). |
| \c mMaxPMTSmdX | 60 | SMD x-strip PMTs. |
| \c mMaxPMTSmdY | 100 | SMD y-strip PMTs. |
| \c mMaxScalers | 128 | Scaler channels. |

\section fpd_mapping ADC Channel Mapping (offsets into \c mAdc[])

Named accessor functions translate 1-based logical indices to physical ADC array
positions:

| Sub-detector | Logical range | ADC offset |
|---|---|---|
| Top (Pb-glass) | 1–16 | \c mAdc[n-1] |
| Bottom (Pb-glass) | 1–16 | \c mAdc[n+15] |
| South (Pb-glass) | 1–16 | \c mAdc[n+31] |
| North (EEMC-shared) | 1–12 | \c mAdc[n+47] |
| SMD x-strips | 1–60 | \c mAdc[n+59] |
| SMD y-strips | 1–100 | \c mAdc[n+119] |
| Pre-shower layer 1 | 1–12 | \c mAdc[n+219] |
| Pre-shower layer 2 | 1–12 | \c mAdc[n+235] |
| South veto | — | \c mAdc[253] |

\section fpd_datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c UShort_t[256] | \c mAdc | Raw ADC values for all 256 channels. |
| \c UShort_t[8] | \c mTdc | TDC values. |
| \c UShort_t[3] | \c mReg | Hardware register values. |
| \c UShort_t[256] | \c mPed | Pedestal values. |
| \c UInt_t[128] | \c mScl | Scaler values. |
| \c UShort_t | \c mToken | DAQ event token. |

\section fpd_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \ref StFpdCollection::adc "adc()" | Pointer to the 256-element ADC array. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::tdc "tdc()" | Pointer to the 8-element TDC array. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::pedestal "pedestal()" | Pointer to the 256-element pedestal array. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::north "north(n)" | ADC for North channel \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::south "south(n)" | ADC for South channel \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::top "top(n)" | ADC for Top channel \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::bottom "bottom(n)" | ADC for Bottom channel \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::smdx "smdx(n)" | ADC for SMD x-strip \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::smdy "smdy(n)" | ADC for SMD y-strip \a n (1-based). |
| \ref StFpdCollection::pres1 "pres1(n)" | ADC for pre-shower layer 1, channel \a n. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::pres2 "pres2(n)" | ADC for pre-shower layer 2, channel \a n. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::southVeto "southVeto()" | ADC for the south veto counter. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::sumAdcNorth "sumAdcNorth()" … \ref StFpdCollection::sumAdcSmdY "sumAdcSmdY()" | Summed ADC over all channels per sub-detector. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::scaler "scaler(i)" | Scaler value at index \a i. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::registers "registers(i)" | Hardware register value at index \a i. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::token "token()" / \ref StFpdCollection::setToken "setToken(v)" | Get/set the DAQ event token. |
| \ref StFpdCollection::dump "dump()" | Print all channel values for debugging. |

\section fpd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
#include "StEvent/StFpdCollection.h"

StFpdCollection* fpdColl = event->fpdCollection();
if (!fpdColl) return;

// Print raw ADC sums for main modules
printf("North=%u South=%u Top=%u Bottom=%u\n",
       fpdColl->sumAdcNorth(),
       fpdColl->sumAdcSouth(),
       fpdColl->sumAdcTop(),
       fpdColl->sumAdcBottom());

// Access individual SMD x-strips (1-based)
for (unsigned int ch = 1; ch <= fpdColl->numberOfPMTSmdX(); ++ch) {
    unsigned short val = fpdColl->smdx(ch);
    // use val ...
}

// Full raw dump for debugging
fpdColl->dump();
\endcode
*/
